{"ref":"BDB, שׁוּחָה","hw":"שׁוּחָה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">שׁוּחָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. pit</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 2:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.2.6\">Je 2:6</a> <em>land of steppe and pits</em> (coll.); fig., <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּרָה שׁ׳ לִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 18:20\" href=\"/Jeremiah.18.20\">Je 18:20</a>, so v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 18:22\" href=\"/Jeremiah.18.22\">22</a> (Qr); <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲמֻקָּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:27\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.27\">Pr 23:27</a> <em>deep pit</em> (in fig. of harlot), cf. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 22:14\" href=\"/Proverbs.22.14\">22:14</a>.","next":"BDB, שִׁיחָה","prev":"BDB, שׁוּחַ"}